USER kit.conductor_run.run. It does not score, diagnose, or decide. It sends
USER nothing and never restarts a stopped job. The conductor is still unbuilt.
USER 
USER Every round record this module writes carries wall-clock stamps, taken from
USER the local zone and spelled as ISO 8601 at second precision with a numeric
USER offset. ``started_at`` is taken once, when ``loop()`` is entered, before the
USER packet is loaded; each written round record carries its own ``started_at`` at
USER the top of its round and an ``ended_at`` taken when that record is written,
USER inside the job window and in order across rounds.
USER 
USER A finish is filed by this module or not filed at all. ``loop()`` writes
USER ``summary.json`` with what the finish says and, for a stop a human must see,
USER ``escalation.json`` beside it, and returns the summary. It files nothing and
USER raises ``CustodyNotDone`` for the one finish it cannot file cleanly: a run
USER whose clock was replaced took stamps that are not this module's readings.
USER ``datetime`` is the clock seam, so a replaced clock is visible here; nothing
USER replaces it in a real run, so a real finish is always filed. ``CustodyNotDone``
USER is an ``Exception`` and never a ``ValueError``, and its ``exit_code`` is 1, 2
USER or 3 and never 0. A packet refusal is not a finish: it raises ``ValueError``
USER and writes ``escalation.json`` with ``started_at`` and ``refused_at``, a later
USER reading of the same clock, and no ``ended_at``. Nothing reads these fields
USER back: the deadline and the clock stop stay on the monotonic clock, so a
USER wall-clock jump changes no stop, state, outcome or round count.
USER 
USER A finish also has to ship a custody record. ``loop()`` calls
USER ``emit_custody_for_finish(record_dir, summary)`` once, after the round records
USER and a ``packet.json`` describing the finish exist and before ``summary.json``
USER or ``escalation.json`` is written. The seam runs ``kit/emit_custody.py`` against
USER ``record_dir`` and returns the emitter's exit code; 0 means the record at
USER ``record_dir/custody/record.custody.json`` was written and names no hard gap.
USER Any other code is not a done finish: ``loop()`` raises ``CustodyNotDone`` with
USER that code and writes neither ``summary.json`` nor ``escalation.json``. A packet
USER refusal is not a finish: the seam is not called and no custody record is
USER written.
USER """
